  "scenes": [
    {
      "narration": "Pull out any banknote. It promises nothing, and it's backed by no gold or silver at all. So why is it worth anything?",
      "shots": [
        {
          "block": "hook",
          "art": "priceTag",
          "props": [
            "bill",
            "x"
          ],
          "lines": [
            "Backed by",
            "nothing."
          ]
        }
      ],
      "id": "s1"
    },
    {
      "narration": "A modern dollar is fiat money. Its value comes purely from trust, not from any metal in a vault.",
      "shots": [
        {
          "block": "truth",
          "art": "priceTag",
          "kicker": "what it is",
          "line": "Fiat money",
          "sub": "value by trust, not gold"
        }
      ],
      "id": "s2"
    },
    {
      "narration": "Fiat money is currency not backed by a physical commodity like gold.",
      "shots": [
        {
          "block": "evidence",
          "sourceId": "wiki-fiat",
          "kicker": "Wikipedia · fiat money"
        }
      ],
      "id": "s3"
    },
    {
      "narration": "Exactly zero gold or silver stands behind a dollar today.",
      "shots": [
        {
          "block": "stat",
          "art": "priceTag",
          "big": "$0",
          "label": "of gold backs a modern dollar",
          "props": [
            "x",
            "coin"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "id": "s4"
    },
    {
      "narration": "So what holds it up? First, the law says it must be accepted to settle debts.",
      "shots": [
        {
          "block": "flash",
          "bg": "ink",
          "line": "The law backs it",
          "props": [
            "bill",
            "check"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "id": "s5"
    },
    {
      "narration": "Legal tender is money that must be accepted to pay a debt.",
      "shots": [
        {
          "block": "evidence",
          "sourceId": "wiki-legal",
          "kicker": "Wikipedia · legal tender"
        }
      ],
      "id": "s6"
    },
    {
      "narration": "Second, and bigger, is that the government demands its taxes be paid in it.",
      "shots": [
        {
          "block": "center",
          "art": "bank",
          "line": "Taxes demand it",
          "props": [
            "bill",
            "coin"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "id": "s7"
    },
    {
      "narration": "One theory, chartalism, says money has value because the state taxes in it.",
      "shots": [
        {
          "block": "evidence",
          "sourceId": "wiki-chartalism",
          "kicker": "Wikipedia · chartalism"
        }
      ],
      "id": "s8"
    },
    {
      "narration": "Trust, plus a little legal muscle, really is the whole trick.",
      "shots": [
        {
          "block": "flash",
          "bg": "ink",
          "line": "Trust + the law",
          "props": [
            "bill",
            "check"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "id": "s9"
    },
    {
